# TEST FIXTURE - NOT A REAL CERTIFICATE. Self-signed, name under .invalid, valid for 100 years, the private key
# was thrown away. It exists because Go refuses to sign with SHA-1 and to generate short RSA keys, but parses them.
# Made with OpenSSL 3.5 (MSYS_NO_PATHCONV=1, key written to a scratch file and deleted):
#   openssl req -x509 -newkey rsa:2048 -nodes -keyout <discarded> -out weak-signature-sha1.pem -sha1 -days 36500 -subj "/CN=fixture-weak-signature.invalid" -addext "subjectAltName=DNS:fixture-weak-signature.invalid"
